<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds were higher in late trade on Monday, in line with other European bond markets in thin pre-Christmas trade, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;We're just following Bunds. There's no-one in the market and there's no volume,&quot; a trader at a foreign bank said.</p>
<p>The auction of one-year Treasury bills, which saw a new historic low yield at 5.800 percent versus 5.900 percent provided no impetus, he said.</p>
<p>&quot;The (March) future's done quite well, but that's because of other markets. We've seen a little switching along the (yield) curve, but there's no news,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
